{"title":"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains 2 red marbles, 2 green marbles, and 2 yellow marbles. Carol takes 2 marbles from the box at random; then Claudia takes 2 of the remaining marbles at random; and then Cheryl takes the last 2 marbles. What is the probability that Cheryl gets 2 marbles of the same color?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1754ee901d55b17d10afc2d9dd7ddec38ede94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{10} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Cheryl gets two marbles of the same color, then Claudia and Carol must take all four marbles of the two other colors. The probability of this happening, given that Cheryl has two marbles of a certain color is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c0258cf72ff2b9745dce23459c8635e17fdfcf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{6} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{2}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />. Since there are three different colors, our final probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263e58b055be7b9aba3fade1cc65509e6118c370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{15} = \\textbf{ (C)} \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The order of the girls' drawing the balls really does not matter. Thus, we can let Cheryl draw first, so after she draws one ball, the other must be of the same color. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad8fedf99f3b28c1444e74fc0cf4b83a9af2a95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} \\textbf{ (C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total number of ways they can draw is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/788d25726850dd8755eb1a94a98eed447b818026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${6 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1da63ca45e9320070351fcb519932dbc54957d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6578a2f580805b3233430d0995a45b39f55ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" />. Let Cheryl draw first and since there are three colors, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53d0493d1324e8925020f6cbafa257c6356a8426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3 \\choose 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways she can get 2 marbles of the same color. The other two pick two each, which leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1da63ca45e9320070351fcb519932dbc54957d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6578a2f580805b3233430d0995a45b39f55ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" />, respectively.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/2015acf2dd7023b776377a0cef07d51a27056338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{3 \\choose 1}{4 \\choose 2}{2 \\choose 2}}{{6 \\choose 2}{4 \\choose 2}{2 \\choose 2}} = \\frac{1}{5} \\textbf{ (C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"144\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As others have said, Carol and Claudia should not have an impact on the 2 marbles Cheryl takes. This simplifies the problem into a total number of arrangements of Cheryl choosing 2 out of 6, and a total number of successful outcomes of 3 (two reds, two blues, and two yellows). This gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e574738a80a5121223d1cd0e66872b0110c59602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{{6 \\choose 2}} = \\frac{1}{5} = \\textbf{ (C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"125\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>~PeterDoesPhysics\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A\">2015 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041435\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 157/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1961/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2610/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.526      1 Template:AMC12_box\n100.00%    7.526      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13958:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041435 and revision id 225712. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}